Tessel 2: trim the mt7620 "spi refclk" pinmux group to pin 37 only (k6.6).

The Tessel coprocessor (SAMD21) sits on the MT7620's second SPI chip-select, which
upstream OpenWrt models as a separate controller spi1: spi@b40 (bus 1). Its pinctrl
references the pin group the .dtsi labels `spi_cs1`, which maps to the stock
"spi refclk" group -- same hardware mode bit as every prior hop.

IMPORTANT DELTA vs the patches-5.15 version (RE-PATH #3): at kernel 6.6 the ramips
pinmux driver was migrated upstream OUT of drivers/pinctrl/ralink/ and INTO
drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt7620.c (the ralink pinctrl dir was removed;
OpenWrt now selects CONFIG_PINCTRL_MT7620=y + CONFIG_PINCTRL_MTK_MTMIPS=y, the
renamed PINCTRL_RALINK). The struct type was also renamed ralink_pmx_func ->
mtmips_pmx_func. The `refclk_grp` definition is otherwise byte-identical:
    static struct mtmips_pmx_func refclk_grp[] = { FUNC("spi refclk", 0, 37, 3) };
so this is the same 37,3 -> 37,1 trim as every prior hop, only the file and struct
type differ. Located by context (patch tolerates the offset), so it applies after
OpenWrt's own pinctrl-mtmips patches.

Stock "spi refclk" spans pins 37, 38, 39 -- enabling &spi1 with that 3-pin group
works for CS1 but steals pin 38, which Tessel wires to the user2 (blue) LED (leds-gpio
probe fails with -2, "pin 38 is not set to gpio mux"). Trimming the group to pin 37
only keeps the same hardware mode bit (MT7620_GPIO_MODE_SPI_REF_CLK, which makes pin
37 the 2nd SPI chip select) while freeing pins 38/39 for GPIO/LED -- fixing the LED
while keeping CS1.
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt7620.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/mediatek/pinctrl-mt7620.c
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@ static struct mtmips_pmx_func mdio_grp[] = {
 	FUNC("refclk", MT7620_GPIO_MODE_MDIO_REFCLK, 22, 2),
 };
 static struct mtmips_pmx_func rgmii1_grp[] = { FUNC("rgmii1", 0, 24, 12) };
-static struct mtmips_pmx_func refclk_grp[] = { FUNC("spi refclk", 0, 37, 3) };
+static struct mtmips_pmx_func refclk_grp[] = { FUNC("spi refclk", 0, 37, 1) };
 static struct mtmips_pmx_func ephy_grp[] = { FUNC("ephy", 0, 40, 5) };
 static struct mtmips_pmx_func rgmii2_grp[] = { FUNC("rgmii2", 0, 60, 12) };
 static struct mtmips_pmx_func wled_grp[] = { FUNC("wled", 0, 72, 1) };
